      "body": "What changed?\nIn _sum_dim_batch_invariant, dims = tuple(range(input.ndim)) if not dim else tuple(dim) treats dim=[] the same as dim=None. Changed to if dim is None else.\n\nWhy?\ndim=[] is a valid no-op reduction (PyTorch supports reducing over zero dims as identity). The old check reduced over all dims instead, breaking bit-identical parity with the real aten::sum.dim_IntList op this function overrides.\n\nHow did you test it?\nHand-traced both branches with dims=(): the float path’s loop becomes a no-op and returns result * 1; the integer path’s loop is skipped and returns result cast to output_dtype — both correctly identity.\n\nPotential risks\nLow — only changes behavior for the previously-mishandled dim=[] case; all other inputs unaffected.",
